It is common knowledge that American baseball is America\'92s pastime. In 2024, the MLB added approximately $10 billion dollars to the United States economy (Levin 2024).\'a0At the local level, MLB teams increase local property value, resulting in a higher demand for the surrounding property (Bradbury 2022).\'a0 Clearly, as the MLB goes, so goes America.\
Given the impact of MLB to the local economy, it is important for both teams and the local government to encourage good MLB governance. The data explored in this paper is vital for MLB teams to decide which players would thrive within the MLB system, the local government who implement fiscal policies to encourage MLB teams to relocate or stay within their jurisdiction, and potential investigations by boffins to identify the underlaying triggers identified in this investigation. Secondary groups impacted by this study includes city planners, health scientists, and economics who may set financial policy or develop the relevant mathematical models.\
